      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2bc57dba_385bcddf",
        "filename": "fuzz/pinweaver_model.cc",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 320,
      "author": {
        "id": 1265562
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-13T18:15:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could look at putting nanopb on cr50, but that will eat up more space and it doesn\u0027t do in-place serialization. The current strategy is zero copy if the protocol versions match which is nice for memory management reasons.\n\nWe would have to upstream patches to nanopb to allow nested callback fields and \"oneof\"s to support this.",
      "parentUuid": "1621e2d6_5c772ecb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 122,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 320,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "536caf38349f6da4c570b80e2c5d6300808185b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88a2deee_b831b9f5",
        "filename": "fuzz/pinweaver_model.cc",
        "patchSetId": 22
      },
      "lineNbr": 320,
      "author": {
        "id": 1135824
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-20T15:53:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the record: Zero-copy semantics are certainly nice, but not a priority here. I.e. in a situation where I\u0027d choose between zero-copy operation and bullet-proof serialization, I\u0027d always go for the latter :)",
      "parentUuid": "2bc57dba_385bcddf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 122,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 320,
        "endChar": 1
      },
